{"repositoryId":1423670109,"availability":"available","full":"Sats100M/farcaster-in-3","name":"farcaster-in-3","description":"Run your own Farcaster read node and client in three commands","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":10,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-17T19:26:15Z","updated":"2026-10-19T14:56:42Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sats100m.github.io/farcaster-in-3/","topics":["farcaster","self-hosting","snapchain"],"demo":"https://sats100m.github.io/farcaster-in-3/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:31.533Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:31.533Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:31.533Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T18:05:31.533Z","stars":10,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The client only talks to your node: reads over gRPC, and writes go to the same node, which relays them to the validators."],"features":["scripts/provision.mjs creates a 4 vCPU / 16 GB server with a 2 TB disk and opens the Snapchain ports. Shows the price and asks before creating anything. --provider azure|aws|lightsail|hetzner.","scripts/destroy.mjs deletes all of it so billing stops.","scripts/node.sh runs on the server. Wraps the official snapchain.sh installer so it works non-interactively over SSH, keeps the database on the data disk, and adds fc-node-status.","scripts/reload-shard.sh fixes a node that skipped a shard's snapshot (see below). fc-node-status tells you when you need it.","client/fc.mjs is the client. Imports a seed phrase once, registers its own gasless app key (KEYADD, no Optimism transaction), then: feed, cast (and --reply), delete, follow/unfollow, like/unlike, recast/unrecast,…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Sats100M/farcaster-in-3/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a9eb3d1e26a19b7f2b2be44d40e5a9bae0c27b212b72f02672284cb800e7cfdb","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:31.724Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:31.724Z","projectInsights":{"vers